========================================
To become the most knowledgeable person in human history about conventional warfare, I would approach it as mastering the entire science of warfare: military theory, strategy, operational art, tactics, logistics, intelligence, technology, leadership, geography, and military history.

The goal would not simply be to understand weapons or battles. It would be to understand how armies, navies, and air forces function as interconnected systems, how wars are won and lost, and why military decisions succeed or fail.

Below is a structured military knowledge encyclopedia and study roadmap.

